=== exp3 v2: fused GEMM+RS (flux sm90 design) vs stock GEMM ===
world 4 (1 process per GPU, cudaIPC), 1024x8192x8192 fp16 per rank
tile 128x256x64 cluster 1x2x1, mainloop stages: baseline 4, ctrl/fused 3 (DMA smem carveout)
epilogue StagesC 4 StagesD 2 (builder default; flux gemm_v3_reduce_scatter forces StagesD=1)
RS pull volume per rank: 12.0 MiB, grid 132 blocks

rank |      base us  TFLOP/s |    ctrl us |     fused us  TFLOP/s | struct   comm  total | pull GB/s | verify
   0 |        200.9    684.1 |      209.1 |        365.6    375.9 |  1.041  1.749  1.820 |      34.4 | ok (rel 0.0154)
   1 |        217.0    633.3 |      224.7 |        377.4    364.2 |  1.035  1.679  1.739 |      33.3 | ok (rel 0.0147)
   2 |        203.8    674.3 |      216.1 |        375.3    366.2 |  1.060  1.737  1.841 |      33.5 | ok (rel 0.0152)
   3 |        199.8    687.8 |      208.4 |        368.7    372.7 |  1.043  1.770  1.845 |      34.1 | ok (rel 0.0152)

struct = ctrl/base: cost of the kernel restructuring alone (static
scheduler, swizzle, smem carveout; comm switched off).
comm = fused/ctrl: cost of the communication alone (flag publishes,
NVLink pulls, fp16 reduction, slowest-peer tail).
worst-rank: total 1.845, comm 1.770. flux pays this to keep the
epilogue local instead of remote-writing (v1 exp3 measures that option).
